INT. SALT MINE ELEVATOR HOIST HOUSE - DAY

Brine-crusted timbers. A cable drum. One lantern. Wind through the slats.

SHERIFF AUGUSTINE "GUS" TREVINO (50s, gray mustache, bad knee) sits on an upturned crate. Rifle across his lap. Waiting.

Across from him, hands tied to the cable rail: LUCINDA "LUCKY" MARROW (30s, sun-cracked lips, torn duster). Smiling. Always smiling.

Behind her, in the doorway: DEPUTY WENDELL OKORO (20s, borrowed hat, pale). Counting something on his fingers.

Gus checks his watch. Puts it away.

GUS
(to himself)
Noon. Should be noon.

LUCKY
Time moves slow in a salt mine.

GUS
Didn't ask you.

Silence. A drip somewhere. The cable drum creaks.

WENDELL
Sheriff. The train's late.

GUS
I can hear that.

Wendell shifts his weight. The floorboards complain.

LUCKY
Your boy's nervous.

GUS
My boy's fine.

WENDELL
I'm fine.

He isn't. His hand rests on his holster. Slides off. Rests again.

Gus rises. Knee pops. He walks to the slat window. Looks out at white flats and nothing.

GUS
(to the room)
Nobody moves till the whistle.

WENDELL
Yes sir.

LUCKY
Hear that? Nobody moves.

She tugs the rope. Testing. Gus turns.

GUS
Quit that.

LUCKY
Quit what?

GUS
You know what.

She lets the rope go slack. Smile widens.

A fourth figure fills the doorway behind Wendell. Quiet. Boots on salt.

REVEREND ISAIAH CALLOWAY-BRANT (60s, black frock, spectacles, a Bible under one arm). Dust on his shoulders. He tips his hat.

CALLOWAY-BRANT
Gentlemen. Lady.

Wendell spins. Hand on the gun this time.

WENDELL
Who in hell are you?

CALLOWAY-BRANT
A man looking for water.

GUS
No water here. Only salt.

CALLOWAY-BRANT
So I see.

He steps in. Slow. Eyes drifting to Lucky. To the rope. To the rifle.

LUCKY
(to Calloway-Brant)
Morning, Reverend.

Gus looks at her. Looks at the preacher.

GUS
You two acquainted?

CALLOWAY-BRANT
No.

LUCKY
Never met.

Too fast. Both.

Gus raises the rifle. Not at anyone. Just up.

GUS
(to himself)
Damn.

A distant whistle. Long. Low.

WENDELL
That's the train.

GUS
Everybody stay put.

Calloway-Brant sets the Bible on the crate. Unhurried.

CALLOWAY-BRANT
Sheriff, I'd sit down.

GUS
I'll stand.

CALLOWAY-BRANT
Then stand well.

He opens the Bible. Hollowed out. A short-barreled pistol.

Wendell draws. Late.

The pistol barks. Wendell spins. Drops.

Gus fires. Splinters from the doorframe. Calloway-Brant is already moving, crashing sideways into the lantern.

Dark. Then fire. The lantern oil catches the dry timber.

LUCKY
(laughing)
Cut me loose, Gus! Cut me loose!

GUS
Not a chance.

Flames climb the wall. Smoke rolls. Calloway-Brant is a shadow behind the cable drum.

CALLOWAY-BRANT (O.S.)
Last chance, Sheriff!

GUS
Come take it!

Gus fires at the drum. Sparks. The cable snaps free and whips across the room, slashing the rope at Lucky's wrists.

She is loose. She grins.

LUCKY
Thank you kindly.

She snatches Wendell's fallen gun. Gus swings the rifle on her.

They freeze. Three guns. Three people. Fire roaring.

WENDELL
(weak, from the floor)
Don't.

None of them moves.

The roof timbers groan. A beam drops between them in a shower of sparks.

They scatter.
